# Shared-node affinity consumer contract

**Activation:** `alwaysApply: false` — when triggers in `agent-discipline-core.mdc` match, **Read this file before editing**. Triggered rules are mandatory, not optional.

How (discovery, GPU index, ingest order): `.cursor/plans/shared-node-affinity-wiring.plan.md`. Per-job cgroup memory consumer: `.cursor/plans/shared-node-per-job-mem-consumer.plan.md`. This rule is the consumer invariant.

## Wire

```text
%jobs jids=<jid1,jid2,...>
%affinity jid=<jid> cpus=<csv-or-ranges> gpus=<csv-or-> cg=<short-optional>
```

Sample header stays one jobid token. Unknown `%` lines (`%begin`, `%end`) stay ignored.

**Detect shared-node contract** from **`%jobs` with at least one jid** — not from hostname, INI, or “this host runs the shared-node RPM.” Sole full-resource jobs (monitor omits both marks when one jid has all online CPUs **and** all available GPUs) look identical to exclusive file-mode samples; do **not** invent membership or `dev=j:` for them **on CPU/host rows**. Exception: **`host_mem_job`** (below) still stamps.

**Monitor mark emit (consumer expects):**

| Case | Marks |
| --- | --- |
| Sole jid on every online CPU (any GPU grant, including none) | neither `%jobs` nor `%affinity`; payload carries every available GPU (monitor M2, 2026-11-03) |
| Sole jid on part of the CPUs | `%jobs jids=<that jid>` (+ `%affinity` when known) on its payload, plus one unmarked `-` payload at the same timestamp with the unassigned CPUs, unscheduled GPUs and node-wide rows (monitor M3) |
| Two or more jids | `%jobs` + `%affinity` per jid payload, plus the `-` remainder payload |

Monitor CPU coverage (`%affinity cpus=`) is the extern-step `slurmstepd` affinity (the job cpuset), not a sample of MPI-pinned task pids (monitor M1). Rows from monitors before M1–M3 still carry under-reported `cpus=` and `gpus=-` marks on whole-node jobs.

## Side table

- `job_affinity`: normal table, unique `(jid, host)`. `cgroup_controls` is provenance (`cg=`), not a cgroup path.
- No second hypertable. Job membership for a sample is `host_data` itself.
- No `host_data` UNIQUE / PK migration. Do not store a jid CSV in `host_data.jid`.

## Stamp

After a shared sample header whose jid is not `-`, non-GPU rows get `dev=j:<jid>` **before** collapse and collapse keeps that token in the group key. GPU types keep hardware `dev`. Exclusive payloads and sole full-resource payloads (no `%jobs`) still collapse to `dev=''` **except** `host_mem_job`.

**Deltas stay per device (2026-11-03):** the feed stamp carries the hardware device as `j:<jid>\x1f<dev>` (`_JOB_STAMP_DEV_SEP` / Codon `JOB_STAMP_DEV_SEP`) so counter deltas key on the hardware device; collapse cuts it back to `j:<jid>` (`_partition_job_stamped_rows` / `collapse_full_cols`). Stamping the bare `j:<jid>` before the delta step diffed every core against its neighbour (jid 79282: IB 1.9 TB/s, NFS 90 PB). Regression: `test_codon_shared_stamp_per_device_deltas.py` (CPython + Codon). Rows written before the fix are repaired from `value` by `manage.py repair_jstamp_deltas` (`--census` first; dry run unless `--apply`).

## `host_mem_job` (job-scoped cgroup memory)

Monitor (`--enable-shared-node-multi-jid`) emits type **`host_mem_job`** on each jid payload (including sole full-resource unmarked jobs). Wire device is the jid; consumer **always** persists **`dev=j:<jid>`** (idempotent if already `j:`-prefixed). KEYS (`U=KB`): `mem_used`, `mem_peak`, `anon_pages`, `file_pages`, `mapped`, `dirty`, `writeback`, `page_tables`. Job-cgroup semantics — **not** NUMA `host_mem`. Do **not** add `host_mem_job` to `host_mem_type_names()` / Summary mem dual-read. Idle `-` headers omit useful stamps.

## AMQP multi-header bodies

Monitor may merge up to 10 non-`$` ring entries into one AMQP body. Attach `%jobs` / `%affinity` to the **digit header block they precede**, not to the whole body. Idle `-` blocks in the same body keep `dev=''`. Regression: `test_multi_header_amqp_body_binds_marks_per_block`.

Listend and sync_timedb (line parse and streaming) call the same helper. Writes are idempotent and fail-open when `job_affinity` is absent. No `/api/affinity/ingest/`.

## Read paths

`LiveJidScopedDistinctHostTimeCount` matches `host_data.jid` or `host_data.dev = 'j:' || job.jid`. `update_metrics` readiness uses the same two keys via `max_host_time_by_jid`. Exclusive jobs match the `jid` column and keep `dev=''`.

**Analysis choke point:** `hpcperfstats.analysis.metrics.lib.job_host_data_scope` (`job_host_data_scope_q` / `apply_job_host_data_scope` / SQL fragment). Wire every job-scoped `host_data` read through it (`jid_table`, TypeDetail, metrics row fetches, `metrics_host_data_sql` when `jid=` is set). PG `jid_scoped_distinct_host_time_count` must stay equivalent to jid OR `dev=j:<jid>` (migration `0037` OR body; **`0038` UNION** of jid-time and `dev=j:` arms so each arm can use an index; **`0039`** optional ``p_hosts text[] DEFAULT NULL`` on both UNION arms — ``NULL`` keeps 0038 semantics). Python `get_live_distinct_time_count_for_jid` keeps **`LIVE_DISTINCT_SQL_PROBE_ENABLED = False`** in production and always returns persisted `metrics_distinct_time_count` (no live `jid_scoped_distinct_host_time_count` from web). **`Metrics.compute_metrics`** must persist Sample Count from `jid_table` / `_JobForMetrics.per_host_distinct_time_sum` (or `get_host_time_df` nunique sum), never from the stubbed getter when the probe is off. update_metrics no longer probes it per row (the Phase A2 healer is retired; late host_data sets ``job_data.metrics_dirty_at`` from sync_timedb ingest instead). The SQL helper wraps probes in **`SET LOCAL statement_timeout`** of `LIVE_DISTINCT_STATEMENT_TIMEOUT_MS` (**15000**) for compose/admin callers. Partial index **`host_data_dev_j_prefix_idx`** on `(dev) WHERE dev LIKE 'j:%'` helps the function’s `dev` arm (migration `0038`) but is **not sufficient alone** for unbounded `dev=j:` EXISTS (full compressed Append).

**Exclusive-host attribution (2026-11-02, `METRICS_CONTRACT_VERSION` 4):** a read-path rule, not an ingest stamp — ingest still never invents membership or `dev=j:` for unmarked samples. On a host the job holds alone, untagged rows in its window (`jid` NULL/`''`/`'-'`, no `j:` stamp) count as job rows, so allocated-but-idle time is measured (monitors before the stepd-title fix tag an idle allocation `-`). `job_exclusive_hosts` decides the set once per `jid_table` window; empty when the job has `job_affinity` rows (shared) or on a DB error (strict). A host is **not** exclusive when (1) another `job_data` row on it overlaps strictly (touching edges allowed), or (2) another jid has a `job_affinity` row on it with `reported_at >= start` — that jid's accounting window decides, and without accounting (sacct lists only ended jobs, so a running co-tenant is absent) it blocks. Index `job_affinity_host_reported_idx` (migration `0044`). Self-heal: sync_acct calls `cache_utils.mark_overlapping_jobs_metrics_dirty` for inserted jids, stamping computed non-shared overlapping jobs `metrics_dirty_at`. One SQL builder `job_host_data_scope_sql_params(jid, exclusive_hosts=…)` serves COPY (`build_copy_sql`, only the batch's exclusive hosts) and the window probes (`metrics_host_data_sql._scope_sql`); an empty set is byte-identical to the strict predicate. `LiveJidScopedDistinctHostTimeCount` and PG `jid_scoped_distinct_host_time_count` stay tagged-only (correlated / readiness counters, not metrics scope).

**GPU (per host, 2026-11-03, `METRICS_CONTRACT_VERSION` 5):** keep hardware `dev`; each host is scoped by **its own** `job_affinity` row (`gpu_devs_by_host_for_job` → `{host: gpu_list}`, applied per `(host, dev)` in `kernels.FrameIndex`). A host with no affinity row for the jid keeps every GPU (the monitor wrote it unmarked); an empty list → no devices on that host; no rows at all → unrestricted. Never merge every host's list into one filter: jid 79282's unmarked 4-GPU node was hidden by the other hosts' empty lists. On a shared job, `detail_gpu_count` and the Summary util “out of N×100” scale sum each scoped host's `len(gpu_list)` plus `Max(gpu_count)` of the unscoped hosts (`ColumnarJobTable.gpu_count_total`), not `len()` of a merged list.

**Residual copies:** host-wide residual aggregates sum hardware `dev` rows. `dev=j:<jid>` copies contribute only when no hardware dev is present, and then as a max, so co-tenant stamps of the same host counter are not added. A negative counter delta is a gap (NaN) unless it is one modulus wrap from the top half of the counter range (`sync_timedb_parsing._apply_counter_deltas`).

**Counter ceilings:** drop per-sample `arc`/`value` at or above `1e13` and `delta` at or above `1e17` before those aggregates (`MAX_SANE_COUNTER_RATE` / `MAX_SANE_COUNTER_DELTA`).

**Memory:** Summary mem / `mem_hwm` prefer `host_mem_job` when present; never add it to `host_mem_type_names()`.

**UI / Job Detail reads:** `is_shared_node` from `job_is_shared_node(jid)` is **affinity-only** (`job_affinity` rows). **no host_data EXISTS** on `dev=j:<jid>` (that probe timed out under portal load and flooded statement-timeout ERROR logs). Affinity miss → False (omit shared footer).

**Job-scoped vs residual types (shared jobs):** Allowlist in `is_job_scoped_host_data_type` — CPU family, GPU (`nvidia_gpu`/`amd_gpu`/`intel_gpu`), `host_mem_job`, core CPU-PMC types. Those keep `apply_job_host_data_scope` (jid OR `dev=j:<jid>` + GPU affinity). **Residual** types (NUMA `host_mem`, IB/OPA/LNet, eth, NFS/Lustre/BeeGFS, block, …) use **host-wide** Job Detail / metrics reads (`host_list` + time only) via `apply_job_or_host_wide_scope`. Exclusive / non-shared jobs always job-scope.

**Residual day-frame cache:** Redis `KEY_HOST_WIDE_RESIDUAL_HT` is keyed by sorted host fingerprint + type + calendar day + rev (**no jid**). Co-tenant jobs slice to their window after load. Ingest `invalidate_jid_derived_cache_keys` also drops matching residual host-day keys. Do **not** share per-jid `job_*_artifact` / `JOB_PLOTS_*` rows across jids.

**Red help footer:** Append `SHARED_HOST_WIDE_HELP_FOOTER` only when shared **and** the surface is residual / non-disambiguated (`show_shared_host_wide_help_footer` / SPA `showSharedHostWideHelpFooter`). Job-scoped CPU/GPU/cgroup-mem / Roofline / Multiprecision omit the red footer. Exclusive jobs omit it.

## Deploy

Migration `0036` and this consumer land before a monitor built with `--enable-shared-node-multi-jid`. File-mode monitors and `/var/run/stats_jobid` stay valid. Prefer consumer before or with monitors that emit `host_mem_job`.
